1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,148
Your seatbelt can tell the difference between you reaching for your phone and you crashing.

2
00:00:04,898 --> 00:00:07,115
So where is the chip that decides?

3
00:00:08,204 --> 00:00:13,390
You would probably guess a crash sensor, wired to the car's computer, like the one that fires the airbag.

4
00:00:14,083 --> 00:00:16,519
But the lock inside a seatbelt doesn't need one.

5
00:00:17,146 --> 00:00:19,777
Pull the belt slowly, and it lets you lean forward.

6
00:00:20,361 --> 00:00:22,205
Jerk it, and it stops dead.

7
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:25,345
And it has to be right every time.

8
00:00:25,941 --> 00:00:29,117
Lock on every tug, and you would fight your belt all day.

9
00:00:29,752 --> 00:00:33,281
Lock a moment too late, and in a crash it's just a strap.

10
00:00:34,344 --> 00:00:38,161
So how does a seatbelt know when to lock, with no power at all?

11
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:41,630
The answer is hidden in the reel it winds into.

12
00:00:42,658 --> 00:00:47,106
And in a really hard crash, it makes a second decision, stranger than the first.

13
00:00:47,609 --> 00:00:50,261
Just after it locks, it starts to let you go.

14
00:00:50,887 --> 00:00:51,839
On purpose.

15
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,540
Imagine the simplest lock you could build.

16
00:00:56,281 --> 00:00:59,592
A ring of teeth around the reel, and a hook that drops into them.

17
00:01:00,329 --> 00:01:02,170
That stops the belt every time.

18
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:04,062
And that's the problem.

19
00:01:04,896 --> 00:01:08,038
Lean over to the glovebox, and it holds you like a crash.

20
00:01:09,183 --> 00:01:10,815
The hook can't be the clever part.

21
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:12,892
What decides when to drop it?

22
00:01:13,875 --> 00:01:15,532
It has only two clues.

23
00:01:16,137 --> 00:01:17,869
How suddenly the belt is pulled.

24
00:01:18,397 --> 00:01:20,203
And how hard the car is stopping.

25
00:01:21,571 --> 00:01:22,733
Start with the belt.

26
00:01:23,428 --> 00:01:25,542
Next to the reel sits a heavy disc.

27
00:01:26,229 --> 00:01:27,595
It isn't fixed to the reel.

28
00:01:28,090 --> 00:01:29,682
It turns with it, loosely.

29
00:01:30,964 --> 00:01:35,001
Pull the belt slowly, and the reel turns slowly, and the disc keeps up.

30
00:01:35,677 --> 00:01:36,615
Nothing happens.

31
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:40,572
But jerk the belt, and the reel spins up in an instant.

32
00:01:41,322 --> 00:01:42,077
And the disc?

33
00:01:42,949 --> 00:01:43,641
It's heavy.

34
00:01:44,223 --> 00:01:45,684
It can't speed up that fast.

35
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:49,012
So for a split second, it falls behind.

36
00:01:50,191 --> 00:01:52,461
That tiny lag is the whole trick.

37
00:01:53,184 --> 00:01:57,477
The reel pulls ahead of the disc, and that gap pushes a small arm outward.

38
00:01:58,126 --> 00:01:59,372
The arm catches the teeth.

39
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:00,568
Clack.

40
00:02:01,281 --> 00:02:02,301
The reel stops.

41
00:02:03,505 --> 00:02:05,688
Does it lock when the reel spins too fast?

42
00:02:06,622 --> 00:02:07,158
No.

43
00:02:07,694 --> 00:02:08,998
It doesn't care how fast.

44
00:02:09,502 --> 00:02:10,789
It cares how suddenly.

45
00:02:11,569 --> 00:02:13,281
The belt doesn't measure your speed.

46
00:02:13,765 --> 00:02:16,394
It just notices something heavy getting left behind.

47
00:02:17,746 --> 00:02:20,254
But now imagine a real crash.

48
00:02:20,897 --> 00:02:24,003
You are sitting still, belt on, hands on the wheel.

49
00:02:24,722 --> 00:02:25,887
The car hits something.

50
00:02:26,698 --> 00:02:29,494
In that first instant, nobody has jerked the belt.

51
00:02:30,077 --> 00:02:31,622
The reel hasn't moved at all.

52
00:02:32,771 --> 00:02:33,701
So what locks it?

53
00:02:34,849 --> 00:02:40,310
Below the reel, in one common design, sits a steel ball in a small cup shaped like a cone.

54
00:02:41,233 --> 00:02:44,126
When the car brakes hard, the cup stops with the car.

55
00:02:44,739 --> 00:02:45,679
The ball doesn't.

56
00:02:46,323 --> 00:02:50,984
It keeps going, rolls up the wall of the cup, and lifts a small lever into the teeth.

57
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:54,487
The belt is locked almost as soon as you start to move.

58
00:02:55,697 --> 00:02:56,832
And it's fast.

59
00:02:57,452 --> 00:03:02,667
Under the American rule, in a hard stop, less than an inch of belt gets out before it locks.

60
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:07,645
And if the car tips past forty-five degrees, it locks with no crash at all.

61
00:03:08,351 --> 00:03:12,130
Gravity rolls the ball, and the belt holds you, even upside down.

62
00:03:13,482 --> 00:03:15,056
So the lock works.

63
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:17,451
And that is the new problem.

64
00:03:18,677 --> 00:03:24,902
Once the belt locks, your body is still rushing forward, and all of that lands on one strap across your chest.

65
00:03:25,691 --> 00:03:28,257
The front of the car crumples to soften the stop.

66
00:03:28,905 --> 00:03:30,474
The belt barely gives.

67
00:03:30,937 --> 00:03:32,065
It's built to hold.

68
00:03:33,211 --> 00:03:34,817
And chests can break.

69
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:39,777
In bad crashes, older people were often badly hurt by the belt itself.

70
00:03:40,611 --> 00:03:43,174
The belt that saved them was also hurting them.

71
00:03:44,552 --> 00:03:46,262
Engineers did two things.

72
00:03:46,873 --> 00:03:47,628
And the first?

73
00:03:48,592 --> 00:03:50,320
Remember the chip you guessed at the start?

74
00:03:51,213 --> 00:03:51,945
It's real.

75
00:03:52,449 --> 00:03:53,783
It just has a different job.

76
00:03:54,875 --> 00:04:02,063
At the very start of a crash, the sensors that fire the airbag also fire a charge in the belt, usually a tiny explosive.

77
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:05,361
It snaps the belt tight and pulls out the slack.

78
00:04:06,089 --> 00:04:12,432
Now your body starts slowing down with the car, sooner and more gently, instead of being caught late and hard.

79
00:04:13,608 --> 00:04:14,676
And the second fix?

80
00:04:15,563 --> 00:04:16,494
It sounds wrong.

81
00:04:17,223 --> 00:04:20,445
Inside the reel sits a steel bar that is built to twist.

82
00:04:21,590 --> 00:04:25,008
In a small crash, the bar holds, and the belt stays locked.

83
00:04:25,705 --> 00:04:29,749
But when the pull on your chest reaches a set limit, the bar starts to twist.

84
00:04:30,465 --> 00:04:33,433
Now the reel can turn a little, even while it's locked.

85
00:04:34,125 --> 00:04:38,263
The belt lets out, a little at a time, and the force on you stops climbing.

86
00:04:38,949 --> 00:04:40,542
It's called a load limiter.

87
00:04:41,736 --> 00:04:46,670
One carmaker, Renault, set its belts to let go sooner, at four kilo-newtons.

88
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:49,964
That's about the weight of five adults on one strap.

89
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,536
And it added an airbag to catch you.

90
00:04:53,294 --> 00:05:00,518
With the two together, those cars had about three quarters fewer serious chest injuries than cars with a stiffer limiter, or none.

91
00:05:01,935 --> 00:05:04,001
But what does letting go cost you?

92
00:05:05,044 --> 00:05:08,426
Every bit of belt it lets out, you travel further forward.

93
00:05:09,144 --> 00:05:11,545
That's why the softer limit came with an airbag.

94
00:05:12,172 --> 00:05:18,604
And engineers worry about tall or heavy passengers, who might let out too much belt and reach the inside of the car.

95
00:05:19,823 --> 00:05:21,171
Where do you set the limit, then?

96
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:24,920
Too high, and the belt hurts the chest it holds.

97
00:05:25,577 --> 00:05:27,815
Too low, and it lets you go too far.

98
00:05:28,595 --> 00:05:30,714
Every limit is a choice between the two.

99
00:05:31,927 --> 00:05:35,419
So in a hard crash, your belt makes three moves in a blink.

100
00:05:36,130 --> 00:05:36,874
Pull tight.

101
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:38,111
Lock.

102
00:05:38,691 --> 00:05:40,440
Then let go, just enough.

103
00:05:41,827 --> 00:05:45,435
Ever pulled your belt all the way out, and then it would only go back in?

104
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:47,410
It's not broken.

105
00:05:48,138 --> 00:05:50,070
Many belts have a child-seat mode.

106
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:57,611
Pull out every bit of belt, let it wind back a little, and now it can only wind in, so a child seat stays tight.

107
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,881
Let it wind all the way back, and it's normal again.

108
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:03,466
Want to feel it yourself?

109
00:06:04,604 --> 00:06:08,780
Next time you put your belt on, pull it slowly, and feel it let you go.

110
00:06:09,609 --> 00:06:12,669
Then give it one sharp tug, and feel it stop.

111
00:06:13,873 --> 00:06:16,853
A disc that got left behind just made that decision.

112
00:06:17,603 --> 00:06:23,714
And behind it, a steel bar waits for the day the right answer is to hold you, and then let you go.

113
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:28,141
Next: the plane wing that is built to bend.
